{"title":"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students taking Mathematics, Physics and Chemistry, no student takes one subject only. The number of students taking Mathematics and Chemistry only, equals to four times the number taking Mathematics and Physics only. If the number of students taking Physics and Chemistry only equals to three times the number of students taking all three subjects, then the number of students taking all three subjects is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c6f98158c3295823e76499a9bfc691306969cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 0\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 5\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 2\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 4\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"341\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of students in Math and Physics and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the number of those in all three. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4977828049d99f20ccd3b4acb6bbd43c2eb70f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> is the number of students in Math and Chem, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89385605cebfe24cd5d7a9402a2908b64a012fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> is the number of those in Physics and Chem.\n</p><p>Adding, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b5177c083a4a7b10dcf881c54df24bbaaacbc5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x+4y=21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />. We're looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f89b21ee7407cc52fc9b48c1a1e84e323b4e97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y\\equiv21\\equiv1\\pmod{5}\\Longrightarrow y\\equiv4\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"319\" height=\"18\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/b/91b53dab189edc1e6e0a55332def7023b0b72395.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le4y&lt;21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/1/7713a88319aa22bdc0476d34d8d998ceba9bd78e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=4\\ \\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2006 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_22\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceu